            <ArticleTitle>'Basic and Applied Thermogenesis Research' Bridging the Gap.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1043-2760(17)30132-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tem.2017.10.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity is a major health problem without satisfactory pharmacological treatment. A promising strategy is to promote energy dissipation by activating brown/beige adipose tissue. However, for this strategy to succeed it requires improving the transferability amongst cellular, murine, and human systems and bridging the gap between basic and clinical research.</AbstractText>
